<p>The person is the picture. A portrait fills the right half of the frame and fades into the ground on its left edge, with a block of the accent behind the shoulder; on the left, a kicker and a title of five or six words with one of them in the accent, and nothing under them — a thumbnail is read at 200 pixels wide. Every <a href="/content-creation/thumbnails/">style</a> changes one thing from here.</p>
<div class="frame-preview" style="--fw: 1280; --fh: 720"><iframe src="/frames/thumb-default/" title="thumb-default" loading="lazy"></iframe></div>
<p class="im-cluster"><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="/frames/thumb-default/">Open at 1280 × 720 {{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a><span class="im-hint"><code>im-studio-thumb</code> · <code>im-studio-copy</code> · <code>im-studio-pic</code> · <code>im-studio-face</code></span></p>
<h2>Anatomy</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Kicker</td><td><code>im-studio-kicker</code></td><td>Mono, the accent, a dot before it: the collection and the length, or the day and time.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Title</td><td><code>im-studio-title</code></td><td>Five or six words, two lines, one <code>&lt;em&gt;</code> in the accent.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Person</td><td><code>im-studio-person</code></td><td>The portrait, right-anchored, fading in from the left. <code>im-studio-person-block</code> adds the accent behind the shoulder.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Corner</td><td><code>im-studio-corner</code> + <code>im-studio-chip</code></td><td>An episode number or the live dot.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mark</td><td><code>im-studio-mark</code></td><td>The square and the name, bottom left, on every frame.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
